Title: Incremental update: builtFromVersion becomes a real watermark
Created: 2026-08-21
Author: minh
Blocked-by: 0003

--- log ---
2026-08-21T13:48Z minh created
2026-08-21T15:49Z claude note planned: watermark persists in a meta table with its backend label; deleteByItem lands on the port in 0002

--- body ---
## Context

`buildIncremental` calls `reset()`: despite the name, every build is a full
rebuild, and `builtFromVersion` holds an item count rather than a library
version. So an added or deleted document is invisible until someone rebuilds by
hand, a deleted one keeps answering queries, and `zotero_semantic_search`'s
auto-build only fires on an *empty* index — a stale one never self-heals.
Tracker: 0001.

Verified on the Zotero 10 local API:

    Last-Modified-Version: 200          one header, one request
    ?since=195&limit=100  -> 3 of 7540  a real delta
    ?format=versions      -> key -> version map for the whole library
    /deleted?since=0      -> 404        cloud-only; deletions need a key-set reconcile

## Design

`deleteByItem` is already on 0002's `PassageStore` port, and the indexed
`passage_meta_item` index is why it is affordable -- 0 ms against 362 ms for
the `UNINDEXED`-column shape 0002 rejected. That measurement was taken for this
ticket: a fifty-item delta on the scanning shape would cost eighteen seconds.

**The watermark lives in the database, with its provenance.** A `meta` table of
key/value, holding `builtFromVersion` and `backend` (`'local' | 'web'`). Local
and cloud version sequences are unrelated integers, so a watermark without its
backend label is worse than none: switching a user from the desktop API to the
Web API would compare two incommensurable numbers and either skip a real delta
or replay the library. On a backend mismatch, ignore the watermark and rebuild.

**Deletions need a key-set reconcile.** `/deleted?since=` is cloud-only and
404s on the Zotero 10 local API (verified). So deletions come from
`?format=versions`, which returns a key -> version map for the whole library:
diff its key set against `SELECT DISTINCT item FROM passage_meta` and delete
the difference. That is one request and one indexed query, not a scan.

**Freshness at query time, not a background poll.** One request for
`Last-Modified-Version`. Equal to the watermark, serve; greater, apply the
delta first. This is also what fixes the stale-index hole in the current
design: `zotero_semantic_search`'s auto-build only fires on an *empty* index,
so a stale one never self-heals today.

**Attachments not yet extracted are recorded, not skipped.** A row with the
item present and no text, so a later delta picks it up. Skipping makes the
absence indistinguishable from an item that has no attachment, and the delta
never revisits it.

## Actions

1. `meta` table with `builtFromVersion` and `backend`; mismatch forces rebuild.
2. Freshness check at query time: one `Last-Modified-Version` request.
3. Additions and modifications via `?since=`; `deleteByItem` for what changed,
   then re-insert.
4. Deletions by reconciling `?format=versions` against `SELECT DISTINCT item`.
5. Attachments awaiting extraction recorded as present-without-text;
   `fullTextSince` already exists on both clients.

## Test

Red step: build an index over three items, delete one from the fixture library,
run the delta, and assert a query that matched it returns nothing. This is the
one behaviour the current design cannot express at all -- `buildIncremental`
calls `reset()`, so today the only way to forget a document is to rebuild.

## Invariants

- A deleted item must stop returning hits. This is the one behaviour the
  current design cannot express at all.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] Add a document, query, find it, without a manual rebuild
- [ ] Delete a document, query, do not find it
- [ ] Add an attachment and open it in Zotero, then find its text
- [ ] Watermark check costs one local request
